commonsenseqa-sample.jsonl — attribution and licence

Source: CommonsenseQA (Talmor, Herzig, Lourie and Berant, NAACL 2019), the
dev_rand_split.jsonl split (1,221 questions).

Licence: MIT, the dataset's own stated licence. The full licence text
follows this notice.

ConceptNet attribution: CommonsenseQA's questions were generated from
ConceptNet 5 subgraphs, and each row's question_concept field names a
ConceptNet concept. This work includes data from ConceptNet 5, which was
compiled by the Commonsense Computing Initiative. ConceptNet 5 is freely
available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike license
(CC BY SA 4.0). See corpus/conceptnet/LICENSE-NOTICE for the full
attribution this repository already carries.

Selection rule for the 100-question sample: sort the 1,221 dev rows by
their "id" field (ascending, string comparison), then keep every twelfth
row starting at index 0, stopping once 100 rows are held (rows 0, 12, 24,
... 1,188). Deterministic — the same rule run against the same source
file always yields the same 100 rows.

